## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Clean Architecture

**100% of business logic in application layer (Next.js/TypeScript)**

### Database (Supabase)
- ❌ NO business logic triggers
- ❌ NO complex functions
- ❌ NO views
- ❌ NO stored procedures
- ✅ ONLY data structure + minimal RLS

### Application (Next.js)
- ✅ ALL business logic
- ✅ ALL validations
- ✅ ALL permission checks
- ✅ ALL calculations
- ✅ ALL history management

**Principle:** Database is "dumb" (stores data). App is "smart" (controls everything).

---

## 📂 File Structure

```
app/
  (auth)/login/          # Authentication
  (dashboard)/           # Main app
    pessoas/             # People management
    times/               # Team management
    projetos/            # Project allocation
    organograma/         # Org chart
    relatorios/          # Reports
    busca/               # Global search
  configuracoes/         # Admin settings

components/
  shared/                # Reusable (dialogs, toasts, empty states)
  layout/                # Sidebar, header, breadcrumb
  pessoas/               # People-specific components
  times/                 # Team-specific components
  projetos/              # Project-specific components

lib/
  supabase/              # DB client (when implemented)
  services/              # Business logic (when implemented)
  types/                 # TypeScript types
  utils/                 # Helpers (format, validation)
```

---

## 🚫 NEVER Do This

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: Business logic in database
CREATE TRIGGER update_salary_history ...

// ❌ DON'T: Direct database queries in components
const { data } = await supabase.from('pessoa').select()

// ❌ DON'T: Hardcoded UUIDs
if (userId === '123e4567-...') 

// ❌ DON'T: Expose sensitive data
return { ...pessoa, salario_atual: 50000 } // Admin can't see!

// ❌ DON'T: Ignore hierarchy
const pessoas = await getAllPessoas() // Manager sees only their hierarchy!
```

---

## ✅ ALWAYS Do This

```typescript
// ✅ DO: Business logic in services
// lib/services/pessoa.service.ts
export async function updateSalario(pessoaId, novoSalario) {
  // 1. Check permissions
  // 2. Validate data
  // 3. Calculate percentage
  // 4. Create history record
  // 5. Update pessoa
  // 6. Log audit
}

// ✅ DO: Use services in components
import { pessoaService } from '@/lib/services'
const pessoas = await pessoaService.list(currentUser)

// ✅ DO: Get user from context
const user = useAuth()
if (user.tipo_perfil === 'gestor') ...

// ✅ DO: Filter sensitive data by role
if (user.tipo_perfil !== 'gestor') {
  delete pessoa.salario_atual
}

// ✅ DO: Respect hierarchy
const hierarchy = await getHierarchy(user.pessoa_id)
const pessoas = await pessoaService.listByHierarchy(hierarchy)
```

